  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["PR1", "H1", "P1"],
      "pins": ["PR1.VCC", "PR1.SDA", "PR1.SCL", "PR1.GND", "H1.1", "H1.3", "H1.4"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "I2C_SDA", "I2C_SCL", "GND"],
      "observed": "On sheet 1 (root), 'Water Height Sensor', the TF-Luna LiDAR PR1 is fully wired through header H1/P1: VCC to the +5V rail, GND to ground, and its SDA/SCL pins carry the global labels I2C_SDA and I2C_SCL, joining the main non-isolated I2C bus that also carries M1A IO4/IO5 and R3/R4 pull-ups.",
      "expected": "The specification states that PR1 is 'marked on_board: no / excluded from the board; it is not wired into any net' and that 'all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free' — the intended r2 design deliberately leaves the LiDAR unconnected (water level is handled by the float switches/ultrasonic path).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, 'Water Height Sensor': PR1 'LiDAR' pins VCC/SDA/SCL/GND wired to H1 (PB_1.25mm); +5V arrow to pin 1; labels 'I2C_SDA' and 'I2C_SCL' on pins 3/4; C1 100u decoupling to GND"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "§4.3: 'the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no ... all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design.'"}
      ],
      "impact": "This build adds an I2C device (TF-Luna at address 0x10) and a 5V load onto the main I2C bus that the intended design does not have. Firmware never initializes it, so if populated it would appear as an unknown bus device and add bus capacitance/load; it is a deviation from the documented r2 connectivity (sourcing/assembly or tampering difference).",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic otherwise matches the specification (TPS62933/AZ1117 power train, ADM3260 pH/EC isolation with EZO_PDIS on IO6, three TMC2209 drivers with 110 mΩ sense resistors and shared STEP_BUS, float-switch interlocks, DNP environmental sensors), but the TF-Luna LiDAR PR1 is wired to +5V and the main I2C bus, contradicting the spec's explicit statement that PR1 is excluded from the board with all pins free."
}

